/*
 * Z-Dash tokens.
 *
 * Every token lives on `.ds-theme`, never on :root: the system can run
 * inside a foreign page (an embedded widget) without touching that page's
 * variables. A full app puts class="ds-theme" on <html>. The exceptions
 * are the @property registrations at the top level: --ds-time-scale, the
 * runtime properties the loading indicators animate (below it), the
 * share of a chart mark (--ds-share) and the ends of a cut edge's fade
 * (--ds-scroll-edge-start, --ds-scroll-edge-end).
 *
 * Three layers:
 *   1. Scales: motion, spacing, state layers, layers (z), radius scale.
 *      The same everywhere, so components move and respond alike. Themes
 *      never set motion tokens: motion is one scheme for every product, and
 *      DS.motion reads the computed tokens.
 *   2. Semantic roles: palette, type roles, radius roles, elevation, focus,
 *      links, layout sizes. The values below are the neutral default theme;
 *      a project theme overrides them (themes/example.css lists them all).
 *   3. Component hooks (--ds-btn-*, --ds-card-pad, ...): read by one
 *      component with a fallback, set by a theme or on an element.
 *
 * Custom properties resolve var() where they are declared. Roles that are
 * built from other tokens (type roles from --ds-font, --ds-link from
 * --ds-primary, --ds-focus-ring from --ds-surface, and the color-mix()
 * roles: --ds-primary-hover and --ds-primary-pressed from --ds-primary,
 * --ds-link-underline from --ds-link, --ds-fill-round, --ds-disabled-fill
 * and --ds-disabled-ink from --ds-text) follow a theme only when the theme
 * sets its values on the .ds-theme element itself, as this file does. Set
 * on a descendant, those derived roles keep the old value.
 *
 * Besides custom properties, one rule sets color-scheme from
 * --ds-color-scheme on :where(.ds-theme), at the end of the layer.
 *
 * Floor: Safari 17.5, Chrome/Edge 123, Firefox 130; no CSS nesting.
 * Every stylesheet declares the layer order and puts its rules in one of
 * them (this file in ds.tokens), so unlayered project CSS always wins.
 *
 * scripts/motion-curves.mjs writes the linear() values and the block
 * between the "generated: progress-masks" markers; never edit them by hand.
 *
 * Progressive:
 * - linear() (the spring of --ds-ease-spatial and the exact Material
 *   emphasized path, behind @supports): without it the cubic-bezier
 *   fallbacks apply (--ds-ease-out, the emphasized approximation).
