     * Every duration and delay is calc(<value> * var(--ds-time-scale, 1)):
     * read it with DS.motion (the computed calc()), not parseInt.
     * micro    press-in of layers and radius, tiny ticks
     * instant  pressed state, popup exits
     * fast     colour, small exits (the default .ds-leave), focus snap
     * base     toggles, exits of panels and dialogs
     * medium   content entrances, small spatial movement (handle, chip,
     *          check), menu entrances
     * slow     dialogs, FLIP, the indicator cap
     * long     sheets, modal drawer, container transform; never routine UI
     * glide    values that travel: progress, countUp() (js/motion.js)
     */
    --ds-dur-micro: calc(50ms * var(--ds-time-scale, 1));
    --ds-dur-instant: calc(100ms * var(--ds-time-scale, 1));
    --ds-dur-fast: calc(150ms * var(--ds-time-scale, 1));
    --ds-dur-base: calc(200ms * var(--ds-time-scale, 1));
    --ds-dur-medium: calc(250ms * var(--ds-time-scale, 1));
    --ds-dur-slow: calc(350ms * var(--ds-time-scale, 1));
    --ds-dur-long: calc(450ms * var(--ds-time-scale, 1));
    --ds-dur-glide: calc(600ms * var(--ds-time-scale, 1));

    /* ── Motion: easings ────────────────────────────────
     * Effects (opacity, colour) and values: within [0, 1], never decreasing.
     *   in-out      M3 standard: effects, on-screen changes
     *   out         M3 emphasized decelerate: the spring's fallback, and
     *               sizes that push layout (they never overshoot)
     *   in          M3 standard accelerate: small exits, leaving fades
     *   exit        M3 emphasized accelerate: large surfaces leaving
     *               (movement only)
     *   emphasized  movement that starts and ends on screen; the exact M3
     *               path below where supported
     *   value       progress bars and countUp(), so figures and bars land
     *               together
